{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"J3 CLOSE ATTEMPT BLOCKED BY THE COMPLETION VERIFIER — and it was RIGHT. Recording because this is the close gate doing exactly its job against MY work.\nBoth Gerrit gates were green on PS3 (LLM-Review +1 PASS, Verified +1, 0 unresolved, submittable=True), so I attempted the close. 'rebar transition aac8 in_progress closed' -> FAILED, 1 unmet criterion:\n  AC6 requires a test pinning that a fitted over-limit value ENDS WITH the marker and does not exceed the limit. My tests asserted only '\"truncated\" in fitted' (a SUBSTRING check) and 'len(fitted) < 200_000' (the input size, NOT the actual cap). Neither proves the contract.\nThe verifier's distinction is real, not pedantic: a substring check also passes when the marker is stranded MID-STRING, which would mean content printed after the truncation notice; and '< 200_000' says nothing about whether the value fits Jira's cap. I treated this as genuinely incomplete work rather than 'satisfied but undocumented' (the verifier offers both routes) — because it WAS incomplete.\nFIX: added endswith assertions for both codecs plus per-deployment length proofs — 'len <= WIKI_DESCRIPTION_LIMIT' for wiki text and 'len(json.dumps(text_to_adf(fitted))) <= _ADF_DESCRIPTION_LIMIT' for Cloud, since Cloud's cap is on the SERIALIZED document, not the plain text. Factored the shared marker into a named constant with a comment recording that both codecs define it independently (the shared layer must not import the Cloud module) but identically.\nPROVED THE STRENGTHENING IS SUBSTANTIVE, not cosmetic: mutated the wiki codec to append 'TRAILING' after the marker. 3 tests went RED including both new endswith assertions — and the OLD substring-only assertion would have PASSED that mutation. Restored, 20/20 green.\nNOTE: the implementation was already correct; only my assertion was weak. So this changed no production behavior — it closed a hole in the oracle that would have let a real regression through.\nVerified after: make lint clean, tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ 1563 passed. Pushed as PS4 (real tree change, so votes are not copied). Awaiting gates before re-attempting the close."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785366536946707001,"uuid":"34eb0099-59e1-421c-b4e3-744097b60543"}